{title: A Cord of Three Strands}
{subtitle: Genesis 2:18–24; Song of Songs 8:6–7; Ecclesiastes 4:9–12}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |
| [Fsus4] [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]In [Bb]the garden at the dawn of days the [Gm7]LORD God looked and said
[Eb]It is not good for the [Fsus4]man to be a[F]lone
He [Bb]made a helper suitable, and the [Gm7]man awoke and saw
This [Eb]one at last is bone of my bones [Fsus4]and flesh of my [F]flesh
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
So [Bb]here we stand together in the [Gm7]presence of the LORD
With the [Eb]people that we love around us and a [Fsus4]promise in our [F]hands
That [Bb]is why a man leaves his [Bbmaj7/A]fa[Gm7]ther and mother
And [Eb]holds fast to his wife, and [Fsus4]they become one [F]flesh
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Set me as a [Bb]seal upon your heart
[Bbmaj7/A]As a [Gm7]seal upon your arm
For [Eb]love is as strong as [F]death
Many wa[Bb]ters cannot quench [F/A]love
[Gm7]Nor can rivers wash it a[Eb]way [F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Two are better than one
If [Bb/D]one of them falls, the other can lift him [Cm7]up [F]
And if two [Eb]lie down together, [Bb/D]they keep warm
Though [Cm7]someone may overpower one a[F]lone, [Eb]two can stand against him
And a [Bb/D]cord of three strands is not [Eb]eas[F]ily bro[Bb]ken
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Set me as a seal upon your heart
[Bbmaj7/A]As a [Gm7]seal upon your arm
For [Eb]love is as strong as [F]death
Many wa[Bb]ters cannot quench [Bbmaj7/A]love
[Gm7]Nor can rivers wash it a[Eb]way [F]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
A [Eb]cord of three strands
[F]Is not easily [Bb]broken [Gm7][Eb][F][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
